~ start
We're at the evacuation center now.
There's so many people here. Most are crying but some are sleeping on the floor.
Nanay keeps hugging us. She won't let go.
I'm glad she's here.
I'm glad Ate is here. And Kuya Dodong, Noni and Kiki.
…
But Tatay… he isn't here.
She said Tatay is strong.
I know he is. I believe in my Tatay.
He can carry heavy sacks of coconuts. He can fix our roof. He can carry me on his shoulders.
So he can come back, right?
…
Every time someone enters, I look up.
I keep thinking it's him.
I want to tell him I'm sorry I didn't sometimes listen.
I want to show him that I'm eight now…that I’m a big boy.
…
Nanay says we should be thankful we're alive.
I am.
But…
Why isn't Tatay here, too?
…
OLLIE:
Tatay…
We're waiting for you.
Please find your way home.
=> END